# ── src/styles/global.css ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The template ships a fixed ~29-line @import chain (Tailwind preflight +
# utilities, the five @takazudo/zudo-doc/*.css artifacts, three @source scan
# roots, and an empty @theme token-override slot) — see #2655/#2660. The
# showcase's own global.css additionally declares ~300 lines of its OWN
# @theme token block (the full three-tier color/spacing/typography system
# documented in src/CLAUDE.md) plus extra @source roots for
# packages/zudo-doc/**, packages/create-zudo-doc/templates/**, src/hooks/**,
# src/utils/** (paths the minimal template's own scan roots don't need to
# cover) and several project-specific base-style rules (find-in-page/search
# highlight colors, version-switcher responsive visibility). Byte parity is
# neither expected nor desired; the separate, unconditional
# check_global_css_legacy_tokens() guard in scripts/check-template-drift.sh
# (#2621, rewritten for the minimal form by #2663) still catches the drift
# classes that matter: a legacy pre-ramp-restructure token reference, or the
# template losing its `@import "@takazudo/zudo-doc/theme.css"` default
# token-set import.
src/styles/global.css

# ── tsconfig.json ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The template ships the minimal 5-field extends form documented in
# packages/zudo-doc/CLAUDE.md's "Shipped ambient type shims + tsconfig base"
# section: `extends: "@takazudo/zudo-doc/tsconfig.base.json"`, `include:
# ["src", "pages", "zfb.config.ts"]`, and a `compilerOptions` block carrying
# only `baseUrl` + the `@/*`/react-compat `paths` (see that file's GOTCHA for
# why those two must live in the PROJECT tsconfig, not the shared base). The
# showcase's own tsconfig.json is a genuine superset, not accidental drift:
# `$schema`, an `include` that adds `scripts` (typechecks the contrast/tags
# audit CLIs) plus an `exclude` for `src/**/__tests__`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
# (a deliberate project-only strictness choice — see the root CLAUDE.md's
# "TypeScript" note), and a `#doc-history-meta` path alias (needed only by a
# project whose `chromeBindingsModule` target statically imports
# `#doc-history-meta` — the showcase's `src/chrome-bindings.tsx` does; the
# minimal floor's default doc-route stubs do not, per spike #2652 Q6). These
# additions are showcase-specific project choices, not something the template
# should inherit.
tsconfig.json

# ── pages/index.tsx ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The template ships a 1-line re-export of the package-owned static index
# route (`export { default } from "@takazudo/zudo-doc/routes/index";` —
# #2503/#2519/#2660). The showcase overrides it with its own brand home: it
# threads `wide={true}` (wider category grid) and an `extras` prop rendering
# the `@Takazudo` link (project-specific, established in #1453) through the
# shared `HomePageView` body's `extras` seam. Both are otherwise thin
# `routeContext` + `prepareHomeData` + `HomePageView` consumers — this is a
# showcase-specific opt-in, not drift.
pages/index.tsx

# ── pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# ── pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx ─────────────────────────────────────
# Both are self-contained doc-route stubs (#2653 Decision 4; locked form
# #2660) — REQUIRED because the injected DYNAMIC `/docs/[[...slug]]` route
# 404s in `zfb dev` (see each file's own header comment for the full
# rationale). The template's copies use only the three sanctioned package
# entrypoints (virtual:zudo-doc-route-context, @takazudo/zudo-doc/route-context,
# @takazudo/zudo-doc/routes/_chrome's createChrome) with no fourth argument —
# `createChrome(routeCtx)`. The showcase's copies additionally import
# `virtual:zudo-doc-chrome-bindings` and call `createChrome(routeCtx,
# chromeBindings)`, threading the showcase's real host-bound slots (search,
# doc history, frontmatter renderers, PresetGenerator, MDX overrides — see
# src/chrome-bindings.tsx) through the `chromeBindingsModule` host-callables
# channel (ADR "Host-callables channel", #2501), plus locale-specific extra
# fallback-tracking props on the [locale] variant. A project that sets its own
# `chromeBindingsModule` diverges from the template the same way — this is
# the documented escape hatch, not drift.
pages/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
pages/[locale]/docs/[[...slug]].tsx
